(A non-print, non-append statement can be the base action of a `but if`
conditional branch.  The default assignment sets total to 1; the branch
overrides it with 99 when the condition is true.)

a number called total is 0.
a number called n is 4.
Set total to 1, but if n modulo 2 is equal to 0 set total to 99.
Print total.
